# src/apps/daemon/internal/platform/system

## Purpose
Host platform authority: transactional DNS/proxy/firewall/TUN mutations, recovery, OS inspection, and platform-specific network adapters.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `platform` (rank 1; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (106): `agent_bus.go`, `android_jni_unix.go`, `android_jni_windows.go`, `atomic_cache_store.go`, `bridge_router.go`, `caddy.go`, `caddy_test.go`, `client_ip_limiter.go`, `client_ip_limiter_test.go`, `cloudflared_argo.go`, `control_filter.go`, `control_filter_exact_test.go` …
- Child folders: `nat/`.

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `system`.
- Notable exported surface: `AgentBus`, `ApplyHostNetwork`, `ArgoTunnel`, `AtomicCacheStore`, `BanDeduplicator`, `BridgeRouter`, `CBTStats`, `CheckLocalTCPPort`, `ChildProcessGuard`, `Circuit` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/boundedio`, `internal/foundation/remoteaction`, `internal/platform/mobilehost`, `internal/platform/process`.
- Direct daemon callers: `cmd`, `cmd/watchdog`, `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/analysis/netintel`, `internal/integrations/relayclient`, `internal/runtime/proxy`, `internal/runtime/runtimecore`.

## Invariants
- Host-network mutations use the durable snapshot → recovery record → apply → verify → commit/rollback transaction.
- Private TUN mutation seams do not escape this module.
- `platform` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
